You are tasked with designing a verilog module that implements a T flip-flop with asynchronous set and reset inputs. The module should take in four inputs, D (data input), S (set input), R (reset input), and CLK (clock input). The module should have two outputs, Q (output) and QN (inverted output).

The module should be implemented using behavioral verilog. You should ensure that the T flip-flop is only triggered on the rising edge of the clock signal. The set and reset inputs should override the T flip-flop and force the output to a specific value. If both the set and reset inputs are asserted at the same time, the output should be undefined.

You should use the following template to implement the module:

```
module TFFSR (D, S, R, CLK, Q, QN);
input D;
input S;
input R;
input CLK;
output Q;
output QN;

// Your code goes here

endmodule
```

reference_solution:
module TFFSR (D, S, R, CLK, Q, QN);
input D;
input S;
input R;
input CLK;
output Q;
output QN;

reg Q;

assign QN = ~Q;

always @(posedge CLK or posedge S or posedge R) begin
    if (S && R) begin
        // Both Set and Reset asserted: output undefined
        Q <= 1'bx;
    end else if (S) begin
        Q <= 1'b1;
    end else if (R) begin
        Q <= 1'b0;
    end else begin
        // T flip-flop: toggle on D==1
        if (D)
            Q <= ~Q;
        else
            Q <= Q;
    end
end

endmodule

