You are tasked with designing a verilog module that implements a 4-bit shift register. The module should have a single input, `in`, and a single output, `out`. The module should also have a single control input, `shift`, which determines whether the shift register should shift its contents to the left or right. When `shift` is high, the contents of the shift register should be shifted left by one bit, with the leftmost bit being discarded and a zero being inserted at the rightmost bit. When `shift` is low, the contents of the shift register should be shifted right by one bit, with the rightmost bit being discarded and a zero being inserted at the leftmost bit.

The module should operate on the rising edge of the clock signal, `clk`, and should be synchronous. The initial value of the shift register should be zero.

