description:
You are tasked with designing a 4-bit logic circuit that takes in 4 input bits and 1 control bit, and outputs a single bit. The circuit should be implemented as a single Verilog module that contains no more than 200 lines of code.

The inputs to the module are as follows:
- A1, A2, A3, A4: 4-bit input signals
- B1: 1-bit control signal

The output of the module is a single bit, Y.

You are given the following code snippet as a reference for module implementation:

```
module sky130_fd_sc_lp__o41ai_lp (
    Y ,
    A1,
    A2,
    A3,
    A4,
    B1
);

    output Y ;
    input  A1;
    input  A2;
    input  A3;
    input  A4;
    input  B1;

    // Voltage supply signals
    supply1 VPWR;
    supply0 VGND;
    supply1 VPB ;
    supply0 VNB ;

    sky130_fd_sc_lp__o41ai base (
        .Y(Y),
        .A1(A1),
        .A2(A2),
        .A3(A3),
        .A4(A4),
        .B1(B1)
    );

endmodule
```

Your task is to implement the logic circuit within the module using Verilog code. The circuit should perform the following operation:
- If B1 is 0, output 1 if the input bits are all even (i.e., A1, A2, A3, A4 are all either 0 or 1).
- If B1 is 1, output 1 if the input bits are all odd (i.e., A1, A2, A3, A4 are all either 1 or 0).

Ensure that your implementation is correct and efficient, and that it meets the requirements specified above.

