Please act as a professional Verilog designer. Create a module that implements a JK flip-flop with the given truth table. The module should have inputs for J, K, and a clock signal (clk), and an output for Q. The output should be updated on the positive edge of the clock signal. The truth table is as follows: 
// J | K | Q
// 0 | 0 | Qold
// 0 | 1 | 0
// 1 | 0 | 1
// 1 | 1 | ~Qold
To implement this module, use always block triggered by the positive edge of the clock. Inside the always block, use a case statement to handle the different combinations of J and K inputs and update the output Q accordingly.

reference_solution:
module jk_flip_flop (
  input J,
  input K,
  input clk,
  output reg Q
);

  always @(posedge clk) begin
    case ({J,K})
      2'b00: Q <= Q;
      2'b01: Q <= 1'b0;
      2'b10: Q <= 1'b1;
      2'b11: Q <= ~Q;
    endcase
  end

endmodule

