description:
You are tasked with designing a module that implements a D flip-flop with asynchronous set and reset signals. The module should have the following inputs and outputs:

Inputs:
- D: Data input
- CLK: Clock input
- SET_B: Asynchronous set input
- RESET_B: Asynchronous reset input

Outputs:
- Q: Data output
- Q_N: Complementary data output

The module should be named "dff_sr" and should be defined in the following manner:

```
module dff_sr (
    Q      ,
    Q_N    ,
    D      ,
    CLK    ,
    SET_B  ,
    RESET_B
);

    output Q      ;
    output Q_N    ;
    input  D      ;
    input  CLK    ;
    input  SET_B  ;
    input  RESET_B;

    // Your code here

endmodule
```

The module should implement a positive-edge triggered D flip-flop with asynchronous set and reset signals. When SET_B is low, Q should be set to high regardless of the clock signal. Similarly, when RESET_B is low, Q should be set to low regardless of the clock signal. When both SET_B and RESET_B are high, the D input should be sampled on the positive edge of the CLK signal and the output Q should reflect the sampled value. 

You may assume that the inputs are synchronous to the same clock signal and that the input signals meet the setup and hold time requirements.

reference_solution:
module dff_sr (
    Q      ,
    Q_N    ,
    D      ,
    CLK    ,
    SET_B  ,
    RESET_B
);

    output Q      ;
    output Q_N    ;
    input  D      ;
    input  CLK    ;
    input  SET_B  ;
    input  RESET_B;

    reg Q;

    // Asynchronous set/reset: RESET_B has priority over SET_B
    always @(posedge CLK or negedge SET_B or negedge RESET_B) begin
        if (~RESET_B)
            Q <= 1'b0;
        else if (~SET_B)
            Q <= 1'b1;
        else
            Q <= D;
    end

    assign Q_N = ~Q;

endmodule

